    "title": "Bobcats hire Taylor as program's newest head coach - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Christian Jones ,\n1 hours ago\nBLAKELY, Ga. ( WDHN )—The Early County Bobcats can now take their name out of the coaching search after hiring Laversay Taylor to lead the program on the gridiron.\nOn Wednesday, it was announced that Taylor would be taking over the top spot, weeks after former head coach Frank Killingsworth left the program to become the offensive line coach for the Ashford Yellowjackets.\nTaylor is no stranger to Early County and its football program; a graduate of Early County High School, Taylor also served as the team’s defensive backs coach, strength and conditioning coach, and head girls’ track coach.\nThe Bobcats will open their 2026 regular season at home when they take on the Crisp County Cougars on August 21st.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDHN - wdhn.com.",
    "summary": "BLAKELY, Ga. ( WDHN )—The Early County Bobcats can now take their name out of the coaching search after hiring Laversay Taylor to lead the program on the gridiron. On Wednesday, it was announced that Taylor would be taking over the top spot, weeks after former head coach Frank Killingsworth left the program to become the offensive line coach for the Ashford Yellowjackets. Taylor is no stranger to Early County and its football program; a graduate of Early County High School, Taylor also served as the team’s defensive backs coach, strength and conditioning coach, and head girls’ track coach.",
